  "Scenes.Dullahan.DullahanStrapOn.WalksPointsPenis2": "[pg]She walks over to you and points her penis towards your lips. She pushes the head in slowly, unsure of how much resistance it's going to meet."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.DullahanStrapOn.WatchesOrgasm": " The dullahan watches your orgasm with a dumbfounded smile, amazed at her own ability to fuck something raw."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.DullahanStrapOn.WeightOnProstate": ", the weight of the dildo pressing down on your prostate, making you shudder with lust and your [cocks] to leak beads of pre-cum."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.DullahanVictory.CollapseOverwhelmed": "You collapse to the ground, overwhelmed by your supernatural opponent."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.DullahanVictory.KnightApproachesScythe": "[pg]The knight approaches you, wielding its enormous scythe. [say: Interloper! Prepare for your RECKONING!]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.DullahanVictory.MorphsSpecter": "[pg]The knight morphs into a horrifying black specter, slowly lifting its scythe, which somehow drips in blood. It approaches you, every movement invoking the soul-tearing wails of the dead, the world blackening with every one of its maddening steps.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.DullahanVictorypt.ForestClosesIn": "The forest closes in. A spine-chilling gust of wind rustles the bone-like branches and lifeless leaves, whispering doom into your mind. You cower. Wherefore, heroism?"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.DullahanVictorypt.LaughAndCry": "[pg]You laugh and cry. Your mind, as trained as it was, cracks under the unbearable weight of this cyclopean opponent. Madness fits you--the sublimity of intelligence."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.DullahanVictorypt.ReapedSoulClaimed": "You're reaped and your soul claimed, a resource for rituals of unspeakable evil. Your quest is over."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.DullahanVictorypt.ScytheCutsAir": "[pg]The scythe cuts the air, dashing towards your neck. You stand at the precipice of oblivion, and even your now-twisted mind cannot fathom the unbearable horrors you'll soon come to know. The scythe kisses your neck, the harbinger of death that laughs at the pathetic defiance of man. This is the end."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.DullahanVictorypt.ShakeThoughts": "[pg]You shake the thoughts away from your head and move to camp. What a night."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.DullahanVictorypt.StrengthFades": "[pg]Your strength, once the pride of Ingnam, fades to nothing. Against this unspeakable evil, you are frail. You have failed."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.DullahanVictorypt.WakeScreaming": "You wake up, screaming wildly, clawing the ground, and scared for your life, but alive. Your wounds are evidence that your fight was no dream, but why didn't it finish you off?"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.FlurryAttack.FeintDodge": ", but it was a feint! You dodge into a position perfect for her to strike, and she hits you multiple times before you can back off to safety!"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.FlurryAttack.RearsBackFlurry": "The Dullahan rears back for a moment, and dashes forward with a flurry of slashes! The first attack is oddly easy to dodge"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.HandleFear.LaughsExcessively": "The Dullahan laughs excessively at your attempts. [say: You cannot frighten <b>DEATH</b> itself!] she screams. Although her voice cracks as she tries to make it sound deeper, she is actually unaffected by your attempt![pg]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.HandleFear.NoPettyIllusion": "[say: You know the things I've seen, [name]. No petty illusion can overwhelm those corporeal nightmares.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.HandleStun.FindsMoreDetermination": "[say: Not... good enough!] The Dullahan finds more determination and recovers from her daze![pg]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.HandleStun.HeadDisoriented": "Despite the Dullahan's head clearly being disoriented, the body still continues to act, though it isn't very precise due to lacking sight and hearing.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.Horror.AbyssIsVast": " [say: The abyss is vast, and it awaits us all. Welcome it, [name]. This is what you've asked for.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.Horror.CowerMorphs": " You cower as she morphs into a tall, revolting and horrifying specter, wailing the cries of the dead in an unknowable tongue.\nBy the gods, you have picked a fight with the horseman of the dead, an unknowable entity of oblivion! You can't face such a foe, it's impossible, it's madness itself!"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.Horror.DashesBackCloak": "The Dullahan dashes back, and covers itself completely in its cloak. She turns around, as if preparing something."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.Horror.FocusMorphing": " You focus as she begins morphing into a tall, revolting and horrifying specter.\nWith some effort, you see past her illusion. The Dullahan notices, and appears to be flustered for a moment as she reattaches her head and returns to a combat stance."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.Horror.HorsemanOfDead": " [say: [name]! I, the horseman of the dead, am here to claim your soul!]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.Horror.SurprisedTurns": "[pg]When you decide to attack, you're surprised as she turns around, holding her head on her left hand, pointing at you with the other. She screams in a terrifying voice as her eyes glow with a menacing purple light."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.Horse.HandleStun1": "The knight stops on its tracks and shakes its head before rearing its steed back to begin charging again. You've bought yourself some time!"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.KickTheHead.EnoughInsanity": "[pg]And that's enough insanity for today. Time to head back to camp."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.KickTheHead.TiredChildishRamblings": "Tired of her childish ramblings, you stretch your legs, run towards her, and kick her with all your strength. She's launched into the darkness of the trees and bushes, and you know her body will have a hell of a time finding her."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.KnightCharge.BeginsCharging": "The dark knight begins charging at you, fearsome scythe outstretched![pg]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.KnightCharge.ContinuesCharging": "The dark knight continues to charge towards you!"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.KnightCharge.NearlyWithinReach": "The dark knight is nearly within your reach!"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.KnightCharge.PrepareDodgeGood": "\nPreparing to dodge is probably a good idea."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.KnightCharge.RollOutOfWay": "Taking your time to prepare to dodge, you swiftly roll out of the way as soon as the knight begins its attack. The scythe merely scratches you, and the knight continues to gallop forward."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.KnightCharge.ScytheHits": "The long curved scythe hits you, tearing your flesh and dealing a tremendous amount of damage."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.KnightCharge.SwingsWideArc": "Now within reach, the knight swings its scythe in a wide arc with a devastating attack! "
  "Scenes.Dullahan.LearnSkill.AskWhereLearned": "You ask her where she learned her rather unique fighting stance."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.LearnSkill.CantForceHer": "[pg]Well, you can't force her to teach you anything. Your pride is a bit hurt, but you have something to work towards now."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.LearnSkill.ExhaustedExcited": "[pg]You're exhausted, but excited over what you've learned. The dullahan is the happiest you've ever seen her. [say: You learn quickly! It's been so long since I was taught this, I'm surprised I still remember the basics. Hah, I feel so alive!][pg]You wonder just how she's able to have this stamina when the two of you just spent two hours in harsh training. [say: I could go for another duel right now! Shame you look... dead, though. Come back here when you're rested and we'll see if I'm a good teacher.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.LearnSkill.PerkCounterStance": "[pg]<b>Perk Gained - Counter Stance!</b>"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.LearnSkill.RestSoundsGreat": "[pg]Rest sounds like a great idea now. You say your goodbyes to the excited undead girl and head back to camp."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.LearnSkill.Silence": "[pg]Silence."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.LearnSkill.TeachTechnique": "[pg][say: You want me to teach you my technique, right?] It's about damn time. You say yes. [say: Well... you did help me get some of the rust off, since there's nobody around to practice with.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.LearnSkill.ThatCanWork": "[pg][say: That can probably work! I noticed you're pretty damn fast yourself. I think you'll make good use of this stance. Honestly, I'm glad I have the chance to teach this to someone. It's pretty much a dead art right now.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.LearnSkill.ThoughtYoudNotice": "[pg][say: Ah, I thought you'd notice that after our duels. It was taught to me when I was a little girl, back when humans were common in this land. As you can tell, I'm not exactly the strongest knight around, so I do my best to be agile. Make my dodges and blocks be as close and as fast as possible, and counter while the enemy is too committed to defend.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.LearnSkill.TwoHoursLearning": "[pg]You spend the next two hours learning from her, as best as she's able to teach. You almost get sliced a few times, but you quickly learn how to dodge at the very last second with the most minor of movements, and strike with lightning speed before the enemy can see what happened."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.LearnSkill.UnsheathesSaber": " She gets up, unsheathes her saber, and beckons you to a duel."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.LearnSkill.YouNod": "[pg]You nod."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.LearnSkill.YoureSlow": "[pg][say: But you're just... how do I put this? <b>Slow</b>. You'd be better off with a standard stance, dodging earlier and finding gaps somewhere else. Otherwise you'll just end up being cleaved before you can do anything. Work a bit on your speed and I'll gladly teach you my stance.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ListenToDull.BodyBack2": "[pg]You look down into the clearing and notice her body is back up, wounds completely healed, trying to find its head. You grab the dullahan's head and deliver it to the body, causing it to jump in excitement. It then reattaches the head to its torso."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ListenToDull.Distressed2": "[pg]The dullahan seems a bit distressed. [say: Right. Well, nice meeting you...][pg]She extends her hand and points it at you, trying to remember a name she never knew in the first place. After a few moments of silence, you end her agony and formally introduce yourself, much to her relief. [say: Right. I'm a Dullahan. I'm going to leave now. Maybe we'll meet again.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ListenToDull.EnoughForOneNight2": "[pg]That's enough for one night, you think. Time to go."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ListenToDull.FidgetsFlustered2": "[pg]She fidgets around, flustered by the interest you're showing in her. [say: Well, sure I am. Probably, I guess. I mean, I obviously can't die and I haven't eaten or drank in decades, so maybe I'm already dead? It's just something you stop thinking about after a while.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ListenToDull.FirstTimeMet2": " since that's the first time you've... met one."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ListenToDull.GhostConfirms2": "[say: Let me confirm this, boss.] the ghost says, leaving your body and launching itself towards the dullahan. It goes inside the pale blue body and then promptly returns. The knight only stares. [say: Super dead, I can't possess her. Strange that she isn't aware of it, though. Normally, dying is a pretty memorable event in someone's life.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ListenToDull.HorseAppears2": "[pg]Before you can protest, the knight's undead horse appears, seemingly out of thin air. She mounts it and leaves."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ListenToDull.KnightDustsOff2": "[pg][say: Well, I just wanted to scare you, but when you actually started fighting I thought I might as well go all the way.] The knight says, dusting herself off. [say: Most imps and goblins just run for their lives when an undead spectral horseman wails and charges at them. Funny, sure, but I haven't had a good fight in ages. You sure showed me one!]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ListenToDull.LongPause": "[pg][say: That's much better.] A long pause happens as she looks at you. [say: Thanks.][pg]Another pause. [say: I guess I'm going no--] You interrupt her, much to her surprise, and ask why she attacked you seemingly out of nowhere."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ListenToDull.NotFirstTime2": ", not that this is the first time you've met one."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ListenToDull.ShouldraJoins2": "[pg]Unable to contain herself, Shouldra decides to join in in the conversation, jutting out of your chest. The Dullahan's brows raise, but she doesn't show the sort of surprise a normal person would."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ListenToDull.SmirkLaugh2": "[pg]You smirk and let out a small laughter. Yeah, heh, you did. A moment passes before it dawns on you to ask her if she's really undead"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ListenToDull.StareHeadUnderstand": "You stare at the disembodied head, hoping she'll understand her predicament."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ListenToDull.TrailsOffSighing": "[pg][say: I'm... I'm the...] she trails off, sighing in frustration. [say: Well. We'll call it a draw.] You stare harder, and turn your head. [say: Well, alright! You've beaten me! Now, can you please help my body find me again?] she asks, pouting."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ManorChoice.DontNeedScythe": "You tell her you don't need the scythe after all. [say: Oh- I see. Well, the offer stands. If you change your mind, you can just visit me and grab it at any time!]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ManorChoice.DontThinkImFree": "[pg][say: I don't think I'm free. I've still done horrible things, in life and unlife, but I have no words to express how thankful I am that you've taken my burden and made it right. I, well--]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ManorChoice.HardToBelieve": "[pg][say: It's hard to believe. For so many years, I've lived under his shadow. As a housecarl, as a slave, as a runaway. And now it's over. I don't know what to say. Just--] She rubs one of her eyes quickly."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ManorChoice.HowToFind": "[pg][say: Thank you, [name]. Here, let me tell you how to find the manor.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ManorChoice.JumpsHugs": "[pg]She jumps at you and hugs you tight. You're surprised, but you decide to hug her as well."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ManorChoice.ManorSlain": "You tell her you've gone into the manor, and you have slain the necromancer after a difficult fight. She loses her breath and widens her eyes in surprise. You think you might even have seen a tear well up in her eyes."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ManorChoice.NotReadyQuest": "You tell her you're just not ready for such a quest right now. She looks down, disappointed, but soon makes a weak smile and looks at you again."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ManorChoice.StandSilent": "[pg]You two stand like that for a few moments, silent. The manor is still cursed, the innocents can't be brought back. But you've given her a glimmer of hope, and that is never without worth.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ManorChoice.ThinkOverAccept": "You think over the question a little, and accept her request. She opens a weak smile, happy, but still unsure if she's made the right decision."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ManorChoice.UnderstandNotReady": "[pg][say: I understand, [name]. This is not something to be taken lightly. I'll be here if you ever change your mind.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.ManorIntro.OldDecrepitRoad": "[say: You will arrive along an old, decrepit road. The path towards the manor twists along and up a jagged hill, where most life has withered away, fleeing from the corruption seeping in the soil. A horrifying sight, but merely a prelude to things to come.][pg][say: There is a place beneath those ancient ruins overlooking the valley, where nightmare takes shape. He resides there, performing unspeakable transgressions on life and nature. He must be stopped. You must stop him. I'm sorry to ask this from you, [name], but someone must brave through to this abhorrent place and finish this once and for all.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.PommelBash.ChargesSword": "The dullahan charges at you with her sword. You prepare to defend, but at the last second, she switches her attack direction, shoving the pommel of her saber downwards, towards your head!"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.PommelBash.DodgePeculiar": "You manage to dodge the peculiar attack without any harm."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.PommelBash.LeftStunned": " You're left <b>stunned</b> by the concussive force of the attack!"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.PommelBash.PommelBashes": "The pommel bashes powerfully against your skull, causing way more pain than you expected such a blow to."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.React.DeflectsProjectile": "The Dullahan expertly deflects your projectile with a swipe of her saber!"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.React.NoActionRound": "You decide not to take any action this round.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.React.ParriesCounters": "The Dullahan expertly parries and counters your attack, damaging you! <b>(<font color=\"{0}\">{1}</font>)</b>"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.React.RunToWeapon": "You run desperately over to your weapon and grab it. The Dullahan stays silent, with a clear look of disapproval.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.RunCheck.StaresLaughs": "The knight stares and laughs ominously as you run away."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.SparDull.GoodIdeaExcited": "[pg][say: Ah, now that's a good idea!] she says, evidently excited. The two of you move to a clearing in the forest and begin combat!"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.SparDull.InviteSpar": "You invite the dullahan to a sparring match."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.TalkCirceOffer.CirceRequest": "You remember Circe's request to meet Evelyn in person, and decide to propose it to her. You think about how better to phrase the question for a moment, unsure of how invasive such a request would be."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.TalkCirceOffer.DontWorry": "[pg]You tell her not to worry. She clicks her tongue and whips the bridle, prompting her undead steed to gallop forward."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.TalkCirceOffer.ExtendsHand": " She then extends you a hand so you can climb as well. [say: Hop on. I'm going to need instructions.][pg]You take her hand and mount her horse, sitting behind her.[pg][say: No funny business back there, alright? Falling from a horse is a hell of a thing.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.TalkCirceOffer.ExtendsHand2": " She then extends you a hand, but soon notices that you won't be able to ride with her."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.TalkCirceOffer.FineCompromise": "[pg]You tell her that's a fine compromise. You've always enjoyed each other's company, so it will be a slow, but fun trip.[pg]You point the way and she clicks her tongue, causing her steed to start a slow trot. You follow alongside her, towards the Volcanic Crag."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.TalkCirceOffer.LaughSmugly": "[pg]You laugh smugly and tell her you can keep up with her steed's full speed galloping. What she should worry about is actually falling behind![pg][say: Oh, so it's a challenge, then? Be ready to eat those words, and some dust too. Point the way and try not to be humiliated too hard!][pg]You accept her challenge. The two of you get ready to gallop towards the Volcanic Crag.[pg]You yell [say: START!] and launch yourself forward, with Evelyn whipping her steed's bridle immediately afterwards. It doesn't take long for the two of you to be neck and neck, two sets of hooves thundering across the woods."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.TalkCirceOffer.LegsSpreadSaddle": "[pg]You notice that, with her legs spread around the saddle, her white skirt is riding extremely high, leaving precious little to the imagination. It's going to be hard to avoid, but you'll just have to try to not grope her during the trip."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.TalkCirceOffer.SmootherThanExpected": "[pg]Well, that was smoother than you expected. Evelyn heads towards her horse and mounts it."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.TalkCirceOffer.SorryGoingToBe": "[pg][say: Well, sorry [name], but things are going to be a bit awkward if you try to ride with me.][pg]Not being a biped is quite often awkward. You ask her if you should just write down some instructions for her to follow later.[pg][say: No, no. I always screw up written instructions. Well, I'll just keep a slow trot so you can follow me, how about that?]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.TalkCirceOffer.TooLongNotices": "[pg]You take a bit too long, though, and she notices your rather lost expression. [say: Something wrong, [name]? You look a bit off. Come on, if you have something to say, spit it out!][pg]The raw question might just work, you think. You tell her about Circe, and about her request after you told her what happened in the Manor. Evelyn's golden eyes look skyward, in thought.[pg][say: So you just go around gossiping about me to other women? For shame, [name]! How am I going to keep my reputation as a terrifying specter if everyone knows I'm just a regular girl?][pg]For a second, you think you actually angered her, but it doesn't take long for you to notice she's only joking. Her wide smile after her sentence was a good indicator, for one.[pg][say: Now, that's curious. You have to understand that I'm not in a hurry to be analyzed by any wizard.][pg]Definitely--not after what she has gone through. You agree.[pg][say: Yeah. But at the same time, she hasn't been too hostile towards you, so she might be trustworthy.][pg]You're not so sure about that. You tell her she seems to keep a lot of secrets, even if she is relatively friendly.[pg][say: Well, you've still raised my curiosity. I'll go meet her. We'll talk a bit, and if I like the cut of her jib, I'll let her check what makes me tick. It's not like I'm not curious about it either, after all.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.TimeChange.JojoSawSomething": "Jojo mentions that he saw something rather curious last night, but he's not sure what; a centaur or someone in horseback, prowling the darkness just beyond the camp. He says it galloped away before he could get a good look at it."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WaitoutDull.BodyBack": "[pg]You look down into the clearing and notice her body is back up, trying to find its head. You grab the dullahan's head and deliver it to the body, causing it to jump in excitement. It then reattaches the head to its torso."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WaitoutDull.Distressed": "[pg]The dullahan seems a bit distressed. [say: Right. Well, nice meeting you...][pg]She extends her hand and points it at you, trying to remember a name she never knew in the first place. After a few moments of silence, you end her agony and formally introduce yourself, much to her relief. [say: Right. I'm a Dullahan. I'm going to leave now. Maybe we'll meet again.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WaitoutDull.EnoughForOneNight": "[pg]That's enough for one night, you think. Time to go."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WaitoutDull.FidgetsFlustered": "[pg]She fidgets around, flustered by the interest you're showing in her. [say: Well, sure I am. Probably, I guess. I mean, I obviously can't die and I haven't eaten or drank in decades, so maybe I'm already dead? It's just something you stop thinking about after a while.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WaitoutDull.FirstTimeMet": " since that's the first time you've... met one."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WaitoutDull.GhostConfirms": "[say: Let me confirm this, boss.] the ghost says, leaving your body and launching itself towards the dullahan. It goes inside the pale blue body and then promptly returns. The knight only stares. [say: Super dead, I can't possess her. Strange that she isn't aware of it, though. Normally, dying is a pretty memorable event in someone's life.]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WaitoutDull.HorseAppears": "[pg]Before you can protest, the knight's undead horse appears, seemingly out of thin air. She mounts it and leaves."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WaitoutDull.KnightDustsOff": "[pg][say: Well, I just wanted to scare you, but when you actually started fighting I thought I might as well go all the way.] The knight says, dusting herself off. [say: Most imps and goblins just run for their lives when an undead spectral horseman wails and charges at them. Funny, sure, but I haven't had a good fight in ages. You sure showed me one!]"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WaitoutDull.LongPause": "[pg][say: That's much better.] A long pause happens as she looks at you. [say: Thanks.][pg]Another pause. [say: I guess I'm going no--] You interrupt her, much to her surprise, and ask why she attacked you seemingly out of nowhere."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WaitoutDull.NotFirstTime": ", not that this is the first time you've met one, in a way."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WaitoutDull.ShouldraJoins": "[pg]Unable to contain herself, Shouldra decides to join in in the conversation, jutting out of your chest. The Dullahan's brows raise, but she doesn't show the sort of surprise a normal person would."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WaitoutDull.SmirkLaugh": "[pg]You smirk and let out a small laughter. Yeah, heh, you did. A moment passes before it dawns on you to ask her if she's really undead"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WaitoutDull.StareDisembodied": "You stare at the disembodied head as it contorts in pleasure..."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WaitoutDull.TrailsOffMoaning": "[pg][say: I'm... I'm the...] she trails off, moaning. You sit on the ground while watching her face blush harder and harder, eyes fluttering in pleasure as the moans shyly. After a few moments, she whimpers and shuts her eyes, meaning that, somewhere in the bushes, her body reached climax. After a few seconds, she opens her eyes, and stares at you.[pg][say: Alright, you've beaten me! Now, can you please help my body find me again?] she asks, pouting."
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WhenAttacked.DeflectsProjectile": "\nThe Dullahan expertly deflects your projectile with a swipe of her sabre!\n"
  "Scenes.Dullahan.WhenAttacked.ParriesCounters": "\nThe Dullahan expertly parries and counters your attack, damaging you! <b>(<font color=\"{0}\">{1}</font>)</b>[pg]"
}
